<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:57:06 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>arts24</category><title>Tom Cruise's 'Digger' divides critics as Zurich Film Festival stars steal the spotlight</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260930-tom-cruise-s-digger-divides-critics-as-zurich-film-festival-stars-steal-the-spotlight</link><description>
This week on arts24's film show, an unrecognisable Tom Cruise takes a career gamble in "Digger", Alejandro González Iñárritu’s new satire, in which he plays an oil billionaire whose company initiates a world-ending ecological disaster. Critics are divided, but is an Oscar nomination possible? Also in cinemas this week, Anne Hathaway and Dakota Johnson star in the latest Colleen Hoover adaptation, "Verity".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3770b5a6-bcdd-11f1-8053-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-AFF-DIGGER-frame-49.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3770b5a6-bcdd-11f1-8053-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-AFF-DIGGER-frame-49.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2dd88a40-bcb6-11f1-a291-25662a7778f4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:47:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charlotte Lam</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>What if art could help you live longer?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260930-what-if-art-could-help-you-live-longer</link><description>
In this episode of Entre Nous, Delano D'Souza speaks to Daisy Fancourt, professor at University College London and a leading researcher on how the arts affects our brains and bodies. In her book "Art Cure" she draws on scientific evidence to show how the arts can transform our health and what her research suggests we should be doing to optimise the benefits.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da185838-bcd6-11f1-9460-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11997098796abd153eee9290-34120449.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da185838-bcd6-11f1-9460-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11997098796abd153eee9290-34120449.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dbec71e6-bcd4-11f1-860a-0977204ef561</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:02:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Amanda ALEXANDER</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ex-TV anchor crowned as king in Uganda after succession fight</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-ex-tv-anchor-crowned-as-king-in-uganda-after-succession-fight</link><description>
A former television news anchor was crowned king of Uganda's Tooro Kingdom on Tuesday, becoming the 13th monarch of the Batooro people in a ritual-laden coronation that ended a succession dispute. Edward Rukidi Kijanangoma succeeded King Oyo Nyimba Kabamba Iguru Rukidi IV, whose death ​last month from ‌cancer at age 34 triggered a feud, with his mother saying a previously undisclosed son was entitled to ⁠the throne.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2120b0e8-bccf-11f1-a0a4-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-224332-224517-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2120b0e8-bccf-11f1-a0a4-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260929-224332-224517-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">267eea82-bccf-11f1-a1c8-05adb662cfe8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:10:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Macron says UK’s return to EU would be ‘excellent news’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260930-live-macron-sanchez-hold-joint-press-conference-during-french-president-s-spain-visit</link><description>
Speaking alongside Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez on Wednesday, French President Emmanuel Macron said that it would be "a good decision" if the UK decided to rejoin the European Union. The two leaders met at the Moncloa Palace in Madrid on the second day of Macron's two-day state visit to Spain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f943f80e-bcc5-11f1-9e59-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T115111Z-1926653752-RC2NTNAIQ2O3-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f943f80e-bcc5-11f1-9e59-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T115111Z-1926653752-RC2NTNAIQ2O3-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9151824c-bcc1-11f1-8b6b-c97e1a67d201</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:49:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f943f80e-bcc5-11f1-9e59-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T115111Z-1926653752-RC2NTNAIQ2O3-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg">© Juan Medina, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Forced landing of Israel-bound flight: What we know so far</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-forced-landing-of-israel-bound-flight-what-we-know-so-far</link><description>
The Israeli government believes an incident on a flight from the United Arab Emirates to Israel, which diverted to Saudi Arabia after transmitting emergency signals on Wednesday, may have been an attempted "terror attack" by one of the pilots. France 24’s Shirli Sitbon takes a look at what we know about the incident so far, with many of the details still emerging.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c476fec-bcc1-11f1-8b3b-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-130114-130743-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c476fec-bcc1-11f1-8b3b-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-130114-130743-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">81540de2-bcc1-11f1-809f-bf8861a6c7c2</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:29:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mixed reactions in Iraq on final day of US-led coalition withdrawal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-mixed-reactions-in-iraq-on-final-day-of-us-led-coalition-withdrawal</link><description>
The US military announced on Wednesday that it has completed the withdrawal of all American troops from Iraq, ending a 12-year mission to fight the Islamic State group. The last US troops left an air base in northern Iraq under a deal between Baghdad and Washington. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69f1cab4-bcc0-11f1-b65a-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-32.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69f1cab4-bcc0-11f1-b65a-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-32.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">27561aa6-bcc1-11f1-9b55-ab09d4b8b084</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:27:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Why is the US withdrawing its troops from Iraq?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-why-is-the-us-withdrawing-its-troops-from-iraq</link><description>
A US-led coalition deployed in Iraq more than a decade ago to fight jihadists concluded its mission on Wednesday, a move celebrated by the country's leaders, but which some fear will embolden pro-Iran armed factions. France 24's Angela Diffley takes a look at the security challenges facing the country and why the US has chosen this moment to take its troops out.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/10f2ba54-bcc0-11f1-a5c4-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-123506-123935-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/10f2ba54-bcc0-11f1-a5c4-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-123506-123935-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">16ca5ab8-bcc0-11f1-91bc-651518c4360e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:18:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Eiffel Tower chief to step down after female staff scandal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-eiffel-tower-chief-to-step-down-after-female-staff-scandal</link><description>
The head of the company that runs the Eiffel Tower will step down at the end of the year after female staff at the landmark building in Paris were excluded during a visit by a Hindu religious group. The incident sparked outrage in France and prompted a staff walkout that saw the Eiffel Tower forced to close for a day.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/52106b8e-bcbc-11f1-876c-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-104410-104523-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/52106b8e-bcbc-11f1-876c-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-104410-104523-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5728bbee-bcbc-11f1-a5a3-571d409b9b4d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:11:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>'Cornell won't, we will': Student journalists 'relentlessly' reporting on university rape</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260930-cornell-won-t-we-will-student-journalists-relentlessly-reporting-on-university-rape</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, September 30: The Cornell University gang rape investigation reopens. But first: students and prisoners protest in Iran "in a rare show of dissent". Journalist Evan Gershkovich speaks about his 16 months in a Russian prison. Bonus: what can we do to be less lonely? Finally, Fat Bear Week has chosen its winner.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f8dc1c6e-bcbd-11f1-a7bc-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17127727366abceb811018e3-32198856.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f8dc1c6e-bcbd-11f1-a7bc-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-17127727366abceb811018e3-32198856.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1d7a2eda-bc96-11f1-b366-8721dbe9debf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:06:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Elitsa GADEVA</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'People have been buying into the detoxification of the National Rally', French politics expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260930-people-have-been-buying-into-the-detoxification-of-the-national-rally-says-andrew-smith</link><description>
A French politics observer says the allegations of anti-Semitism against the head of France's far-right National Rally have really damaged the party. Andrew Smith from Queen Mary University of London says people have been buying into the detoxification of the party, despite its legacy as an anti-Semitic and racist outfit. But that makes this week's allegations against Jordan Bardella even more shocking. Bardella is accused by the investigative news website Mediapart of sending a series of anti-Semitic remarks from 2013 to 2015. Andrew Smith spoke to us in Perspective.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e28ce7e-bcc6-11f1-8320-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-18021169836abcf9b1ecf558-15827062.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e28ce7e-bcc6-11f1-8320-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-18021169836abcf9b1ecf558-15827062.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cfe5ee94-bcad-11f1-ae9a-85894dbbb5b4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:58:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Medicine prices soar in Iran as US blockade and sanctions hit hard</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-medicine-prices-soar-in-iran-as-us-blockade-and-sanctions-hit-hard</link><description>
Medication prices are soaring in Iran and some treatments have become hard to find, leaving patients and their families scrambling as a US blockade and stepped-up sanctions squeeze the country's pharmaceuticals industry.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec07580a-bcb8-11f1-ba2b-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-103944-104135-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ec07580a-bcb8-11f1-ba2b-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-103944-104135-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f12d46e6-bcb8-11f1-85d5-c9be80049428</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:39:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Argentina shuns meat as purchasing plummets under Milei</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-argentina-shuns-meat-as-purchasing-plummets-under-milei</link><description>
In Argentina, a nation of meat lovers par excellence, where barbecuing is a ritual central to the national identity and the steaks are among the best in the world, meat consumption has now reached an all-time low. The reason: the drastic decline in purchasing power for most Argentines since Javier Milei took office. Our reporters explain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e60ceba-bcb8-11f1-b3f7-1b050e7dec5f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-103639-103833-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e60ceba-bcb8-11f1-b3f7-1b050e7dec5f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-103639-103833-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a33deaee-bcb8-11f1-a73a-e77f3d3b852e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:37:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'A face lift once a month': Growing pressure to conform amid the rise of Korea's 'K-Beauty'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-a-face-lift-once-a-month-growing-pressure-to-conform-amid-the-rise-of-korea-s-k-beauty</link><description>
In the last ten years, South Korea has established itself as a powerhouse of beauty and cosmetics. But, behind the innovative creams, serums, and treatments that have allowed so-called K-beauty to conquer the world, Korean society has also felt the impacts, and people now face rising social pressure to conform to new beauty standards. France 24’s Christina Yoon, Mélodie Sforza and Jan Camezind Broomby sent this report from Seoul.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2888ea68-bcb5-11f1-9c08-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-102345-102547-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2888ea68-bcb5-11f1-9c08-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-102345-102547-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2e15a6c4-bcb5-11f1-b848-012218203daf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:35:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Man City scandal: 'Sham' deals and inflated revenues</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-man-city-scandal-sham-deals-and-inflated-revenues</link><description>
In what may be the biggest financial scandal in Premier League history, Manchester City have been found guilty of using "sham" commercial contracts as part of schemes to inflate revenue and understate costs by more than £900 million over nearly a decade, the Premier League said on Tuesday.  The club, which denies wrongdoing, said in a statement that it would appeal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/062d83c6-bcb4-11f1-a8d6-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-102129-102312-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/062d83c6-bcb4-11f1-a8d6-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-102129-102312-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0bac37f2-bcb4-11f1-a28f-8d91cf9e8b8f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:34:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Was Netanyahu warned of October 7 Hamas attacks?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-was-netanyahu-warned-of-october-7-hamas-attacks</link><description>
Benjamin Netanyahu travelled secretly to the United Arab Emirates over the weekend, Israeli media has reported, to ask its leader to deny claims he had warned the Israeli prime minister about a looming Hamas threat ahead of the Palestinian militant group's Oct. 7, 2023 attack on southern Israel. Netanyahu himself has confirmed making the secret trip, but denies he urged his UAE counterpart to do anything of the kind. France 24’s Douglas Herbert takes a closer look.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/429de330-bcb1-11f1-859d-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-101334-101848-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/429de330-bcb1-11f1-859d-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-101334-101848-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4850074a-bcb1-11f1-ad2e-19f2ba751e32</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:12:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Fatima Ezzahra El Mansouri named Morocco's first woman PM</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-fatima-ezzahra-el-mansouri-named-morocco-s-first-woman-pm</link><description>
The king of Morocco on Tuesday named Marrakesh mayor Fatima Ezzahra El Mansouri the country's first woman prime minister after her centre-right Authenticity and Modernity Party (PAM) party won last week's parliamentary elections. El Mansouri joined the PAM in 2008 and was also the first woman to serve as mayor of Marrakesh, winning the office in 2009 before losing it six years later, then retaking it again in 2021.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0f28544-bcb1-11f1-aa54-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-101915-102055-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0f28544-bcb1-11f1-aa54-098db7fa8bc7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-101915-102055-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f6a3511c-bcb1-11f1-872e-2d8242059718</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:56:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Ethiopia's last Jews dream of visa for Israel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260930-ethiopia-s-last-jews-dream-of-visa-for-israel</link><description>
Ethiopia has one of the oldest Jewish communities in the world, rumoured to be the descendants of the Queen of Sheba and King Solomon in 950 BC. From the 1970s to 1990s, this community known as Beta Israel was persecuted under the Communist regime, and Israel evacuated more than 20,000 Ethiopian Jews in dramatic airlifts known as Operation Solomon and Operation Moses. But a few thousand were left behind.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffb1ae56-bcb2-11f1-a442-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9486861776abcd9182b3702-78110521.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffb1ae56-bcb2-11f1-a442-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9486861776abcd9182b3702-78110521.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0de2f766-bc1b-11f1-b81a-63c1cce5870a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:55:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Tom CANETTI</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tensions mount as South Korea demands apology from North over mine blast</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-tensions-mount-as-south-korea-demands-apology-from-north-over-mine-blast</link><description>
North Korea has this Wednesday rejected accusations that it planted the mines that injured three South Korean soldiers in the DMZ on September 21. In a statement, Kim Jo Jong, Kim Jong Un's powerful sister, threatened retaliation against the south if there is any escalation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d83f03c-bca9-11f1-b09e-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-101121-101248-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d83f03c-bca9-11f1-b09e-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-101121-101248-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">327fe172-bca9-11f1-ab7d-675472ec202b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:14:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Attention turns to economy on final day of Macron’s visit to Spain</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-attention-turns-to-economy-on-final-day-of-macron-s-visit-to-spain</link><description>
President Emmanuel Macron is in Spain for the final day of his two-day state visit, the first by a French president to the country since 2009. After being welcomed with a banquet at the Royal Palace by King Felipe VI on Tuesday, on today's agenda is the opening of the Franco-Spanish economic forum and a meeting with Spain's leftist Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez. Once economically ahead of Spain, France is now seeing Spain grow faster, as the Spanish economy has outpaced its French neighbour in recent years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d59e5d2-bca8-11f1-a80c-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-100847-101046-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d59e5d2-bca8-11f1-a80c-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-100847-101046-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">22f4eaa0-bca8-11f1-bf3e-151e6c4cb332</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:13:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump puts trust in AI bosses to 'police themselves'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-trump-puts-trust-in-ai-bosses-to-police-themselves</link><description>
As fears mount over the safety of rapidly advancing AI models, US President Donald Trump gathered tech leaders at the White House on Tuesday where he said they signed a "morally binding" commitment to self-regulate and build adequate safeguards on the fast-moving technology.  "They're going to police themselves," Trump said after the meeting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b33e092-bca7-11f1-bebc-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-100512-100658-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b33e092-bca7-11f1-bebc-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-100512-100658-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">71256a84-bca7-11f1-a793-992ef8a85733</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:42:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘The country has become a battlefield’: Last US troops exit Iraq</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260930-the-country-has-become-a-battlefield-last-us-troops-exit-iraq</link><description>
The last US troops in Iraq, part of a coalition to fight the Islamic State group, were slated to leave the country on Wednesday under an agreement between Baghdad and Washington. As the Iraqi army officially takes over the coalition’s remaining bases, the government is seeking to strengthen its military capabilities and reaffirm its sovereignty. Meanwhile, some living near the US bases who have been caught in the crossfire of attacks are hoping for a fresh start. Our journalists Amar el-Hameedawi, Marie-Charlotte Roupie and Laurent Berstecher sent this report from Iraq.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9a8425c-bca5-11f1-bbff-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-090255-090517-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9a8425c-bca5-11f1-bbff-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-090255-090517-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ff2db37e-bca5-11f1-ae75-4f23e289f279</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:34:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Netanyahu says Israel is preparing for other ‘potential threats’ after pilot tried to crash plane</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260930-israel-bound-flight-diverted-to-saudi-arabia-after-brawl-between-pilots</link><description>
A flight from Dubai to Israel made an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia after a brawl broke out in the cockpit, with the pilots hospitalised due to injuries upon arrival, a statement by the international airport of Tabuk reported Wednesday. Israel’s Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said that one pilot had allegedly stabbed the other and attempted to crash the plane.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9de8a560-bca5-11f1-b941-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273268796814.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9de8a560-bca5-11f1-b941-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273268796814.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2e0203c-bca6-11f1-b79e-91afbb6948b5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:25:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9de8a560-bca5-11f1-b941-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273268796814.jpg">© Malak Harb, AP file picture</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Ian Bremmer: 'We have passed peak Trump in terms of disruption on the global stage'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260930-ian-bremmer-we-have-passed-peak-trump-in-terms-of-disruption-on-the-global-stage</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Ian Bremmer, the American political scientist, author, and founder and president of Eurasia Group and GZERO Media. According to Bremmer, we may now be entering the autumn of the "Donroe Doctrine" and the MAGA era: an "America First" isolationist approach in which President Donald Trump envisions a return to "greatness" in Gilded Age fashion. But is this the America voters had envisioned?
